  "text": "This study focuses on the relationship between ABSI and diabetes, utilizing data from the NHANES database to perform multivariate linear regression analysis, aiming to deepen our understanding of ABSI as a tool for predicting disease risk. As the global prevalence of diabetes continues to rise, developing effective risk prediction and management strategies becomes particularly crucial. Traditional risk assessment indicators like BMI, though widely used, have increasingly shown limitations in predicting diabetes and its complications, especially as they fail to accurately reflect the risk of abdominal obesity [24\u201327]. The introduction of ABSI offers a new perspective in addressing this issue. Unlike BMI, ABSI considers the ratio of WC to height and weight, more effectively capturing the risk of central obesity, which is vital for the prevention and management of diabetes [15, 25].",
